      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceNeoFOAM_1_1detail_1a6dafaf5a570ffdf46e84fc09a5670401" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>bool &amp;</type>
        <definition>bool &amp; NeoFOAM::detail::faithfulFreestream</definition>
        <argsstring>()</argsstring>
        <name>faithfulFreestream</name>
        <qualifiedname>NeoFOAM::detail::faithfulFreestream</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Whether the far-field family is translated faithfully instead of approximated. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Off by default: the approximations below (freestreamVelocity as a fixedValue, freestreamPressure as zeroGradient) keep the pressure problem well posed for solvers that hand the boundary conditions no flux or velocity context, which is what the incompressible solvers do. A solver that passes <computeroutput>U</computeroutput> in its BoundaryContext (neorhoPimpleFoam) switches this on and gets <ref refid="namespaceNeoN" kindref="compound">NeoN</ref>&apos;s freestreamVelocity / freestreamPressure, which follow OpenFOAM&apos;s flow-direction blend. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/home/runner/work/NeoFOAM/NeoFOAM/include/NeoFOAM/auxiliary/readers.hpp" line="33" column="6" declfile="/home/runner/work/NeoFOAM/NeoFOAM/include/NeoFOAM/auxiliary/readers.hpp" declline="33" declcolumn="6"/>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceNeoFOAM_1_1detail_1a2f0eec60b1c730f1f28d6bf8bd1fbf0f" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>NeoN::scalar</type>
        <definition>NeoN::scalar NeoFOAM::detail::tokenAsScalar</definition>
        <argsstring>(NeoN::TokenList &amp;tokenList, std::size_t idx)</argsstring>
        <name>tokenAsScalar</name>
        <qualifiedname>NeoFOAM::detail::tokenAsScalar</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>NeoN::TokenList &amp;</type>
          <declname>tokenList</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>std::size_t</type>
          <declname>idx</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Promote a single TokenList entry to a NeoN::scalar regardless of whether OpenFOAM&apos;s lexer classified it as a SCALAR (double) or a LABEL (int). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>OpenFOAM tokenizes numeric primitives per token: a literal with a decimal point (e.g. <computeroutput>0.1</computeroutput>) becomes a SCALAR while a bare integer (e.g. <computeroutput>0</computeroutput>) becomes a LABEL. The components of a single vector value can therefore have different stored types — <computeroutput>uniform (0.1 0 0)</computeroutput> yields [scalar, label, label]. A strict <computeroutput>TokenList::get&lt;NeoN::scalar&gt;</computeroutput> throws <computeroutput>bad_any_cast</computeroutput> on the label components, so each component must be probed and promoted independently. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
