      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="function" id="namespaceNeoFOAM_1_1detail_1a7b065272d1172aa5e526974471dea410" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>NeoN::scalar</type>
        <definition>NeoN::scalar NeoFOAM::detail::dictEntryAsScalar</definition>
        <argsstring>(const NeoN::Dictionary &amp;dict, const std::string &amp;key)</argsstring>
        <name>dictEntryAsScalar</name>
        <qualifiedname>NeoFOAM::detail::dictEntryAsScalar</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const NeoN::Dictionary &amp;</type>
          <declname>dict</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>key</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Read a plain (non-stream) numeric dictionary entry as a NeoN::scalar. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Mirrors tokenAsScalar&apos;s reasoning for an entry that is not wrapped in a TokenList at all — e.g. waveTransmissive&apos;s bare <computeroutput>gamma 1.4;</computeroutput>/<computeroutput>fieldInf 101325;</computeroutput> entries, written directly by writeEntry() rather than through a <computeroutput>uniform &lt;value&gt;</computeroutput>-style stream. A literal with no decimal point (e.g. <computeroutput>101325</computeroutput>) tokenizes as a label, so <computeroutput><ref refid="namespaceNeoFOAM_1af69b228bd9e492814da093da0a51d1ac" kindref="member">convert()</ref></computeroutput> stores it as NeoN::label rather than NeoN::scalar; this promotes either representation to NeoN::scalar. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
