        <name>constantFunction1AsScalar</name>
        <qualifiedname>NeoFOAM::detail::constantFunction1AsScalar</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>const NeoN::Dictionary &amp;</type>
          <declname>dict</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const std::string &amp;</type>
          <declname>key</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Read an OpenFOAM Function1&lt;scalar&gt; entry that is a constant, as a NeoN::scalar. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>A constant Function1 is written as <computeroutput>&lt;key&gt; constant &lt;value&gt;;</computeroutput> (OpenFOAM&apos;s own <ref refid="namespaceNeoFOAM_1a0fdc041fbcfcb89b3d2f87395606b3c7" kindref="member">write()</ref>) and may be given as a bare <computeroutput>&lt;key&gt; &lt;value&gt;;</computeroutput>. Any other Function1 (table, sine, ramp, ...) depends on time, which the boundary conditions this is used for (fixedMean&apos;s meanValue, flowRateInletVelocity&apos;s flow rate) do not model. Taking such an entry as a constant would silently prescribe the wrong flow, so it is an error. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
